# ─── Environment Variables ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit the actual .env file — use .env.example as the template
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.production

# ─── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ─── Uploaded Files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local avatar uploads should not be tracked in git.
# In production these will move to Cloudinary.
uploads/*
!uploads/.gitkeep

# ─── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ─── OS Files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Editor / IDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln

# ─── Coverage & Testing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
```

Also create an empty `.gitkeep` file inside `uploads/` so the folder itself is tracked by git (keeping the folder structure intact for new contributors) even though its contents are ignored:

**File:** `SkillSwap_MERN/backend/uploads/.gitkeep`

```